    "Scouting Notes": "Potential top prospect in baseball by 2023\n Youngest player in full season ball by a good margin.\n Off to one of the best full season ball starts of any 18 year old in the last couple of decades. \n Covers all areas of the strike zone. \n Approach has varied a bit. Early, he swung and missed at high FB a lot. Later he had some trouble with spin down and away.\n Change to toe tap helped reach high FB, mental awareness that pitchers were throwing more breaking balls has helped with that.\n Showing a great ability to adjust to what pitchers are doing against him.\n Drives the ball to all fields, and does so in all counts. \n Elevates the ball a lot. \n Big time exit velos, both at peak (110 MPH) and for his average exit velos (around 90 MPH average).\n Hard hit rate of over 45% (95+ MPH exit velos) \n Has tools to steal 30+ bases and be an above average center fielder. \n Can be one of the best offensive prospects the Brewers organization has ever seen.",
